The '''gin basil smash''' is a cocktail consisting of [[gin]], lemon juice, simple syrup, and Genovese basil.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Gin Basil Smash |url=https://iba-world.com/iba-cocktail/gin-basil-smash/ |access-date=29 July 2025 |website=International Bartenders Association}}</ref> It is a type of [[List of cocktails#Smashed fruit|smash]], a cocktail made of muddled fruit or herbs.

== History ==
The gin basil smash was created in 2008 by German bartender Jörg Meyer. Meyer first created and served the drink at his bar, Le Lion, in [[Hamburg]], [[Germany]]. The gin basil smash was inspired by the Whiskey Smash. Meyer initially sold the drink as Gin Pesto before changing it to its current name.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Simonson |first=Robert |date=28 June 2021 |title=How the Gin Basil Smash Became a Modern Classic |url=https://punchdrink.com/articles/how-gin-basil-smash-became-modern-classic-cocktail-recipe-le-lion/ |access-date=30 July 2025 |website=Punch |language=en}}</ref>

== Preparation ==
The [[International Bartenders Association]] prescribes that all ingredients should be shaken in a shaker tin and then strained into a chilled cocktail glass.<ref name=":0" /> The drink may also be served [[Bartending terminology|on the rocks]], rather than straight up, and garnished with a sprig of basil.<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=epOZ5jGEZwM |title=Gin-Basil Smash cocktail by Jörg Meyer |date=24 April 2009 |last=jayhepburn |access-date=30 July 2025 |via=YouTube}}</ref>

